# `.ics` content lines are CRLF-terminated by RFC 5545 §3.1, and these
# fixtures exist to reproduce what a real calendar client emits. Without
# `-text` the repo's `core.autocrlf=input` normalises them to LF on commit,
# and the CRLF path stops being exercised by anything but a synthetic string
# in a unit test.
*.ics -text
